273
00:21:05,805 --> 00:21:14,908
[SPEAKER_01]: I'm just wondering about the house that's highlighted here, notable, and one of the ones that we concentrate on, and I understand the district idea.

274
00:21:15,568 --> 00:21:20,070
[SPEAKER_08]: Most of the people who own, with one exception, that's 33 Forest,

275
00:21:22,014 --> 00:21:28,237
[SPEAKER_08]: Most of the people who own historic houses are not against the historic district.

276
00:21:29,938 --> 00:21:34,840
[SPEAKER_08]: Now, I wouldn't say, I wouldn't go, I wouldn't state it in terms of the converse.

277
00:21:35,880 --> 00:21:37,561
[SPEAKER_08]: I'm not sure, we don't know.

278
00:21:38,461 --> 00:21:42,143
[SPEAKER_08]: Most of the, a lot of the owners of historic houses didn't respond.

279
00:21:42,183 --> 00:21:46,905
[SPEAKER_08]: So we don't know what they think, but at least they had a chance to respond and they were not against it.

280
00:21:49,907 --> 00:21:50,127
[SPEAKER_08]: So,

281
00:21:52,190 --> 00:21:59,293
[SPEAKER_08]: I sent, did I send you that list of my breakdown of the houses by address?

