00:22:11,159 --> 00:22:11,859
[SPEAKER_08]: Yes, beautiful.

287
00:22:12,160 --> 00:22:16,642
[SPEAKER_08]: This is, Fred did this before I sent out the detailed breakdown.

288
00:22:17,728 --> 00:22:25,212
[SPEAKER_01]: It's funny, I'm starting to fall in love with Water Street, Ashland Place, Chestnut, some beautiful properties in there as well.

289
00:22:25,272 --> 00:22:27,453
[SPEAKER_08]: Sure, but we need to stay focused on that.

290
00:22:27,553 --> 00:22:28,414
[SPEAKER_01]: Understood, understood.

291
00:22:28,814 --> 00:22:29,114
[SPEAKER_08]: Okay.

292
00:22:29,774 --> 00:22:42,241
[SPEAKER_08]: Basically, all the takeaway, my takeaway from my specific analysis was that everyone who lives in a house that has Form B,

293
00:22:46,133 --> 00:22:49,094
[SPEAKER_08]: There's no one who lives in a house that has a form B that is against it.

294
00:22:50,634 --> 00:23:06,118
[SPEAKER_08]: And there is no one who's against it that lives in a house with a form B. So maybe we can use form B as kind of decision or anyway.

295
00:23:07,018 --> 00:23:09,179
[SPEAKER_08]: So Fred has a quite independent proposal.

296
00:23:09,219 --> 00:23:13,340
[SPEAKER_08]: He proposed just paring down for us the forestry district to,

