00:27:57,028 --> 00:28:07,037
[SPEAKER_08]: Let's go on to our next agenda item, which is

339
00:28:09,455 --> 00:28:13,879
[SPEAKER_08]: possible local historic district for 78 Cotting Street.

340
00:28:14,819 --> 00:28:26,268
[SPEAKER_08]: Now, let me, we have the owners here and we have a resident here who is interested in creating a single local house historic district for 78 Cotting.

341
00:28:27,189 --> 00:28:38,118
[SPEAKER_08]: But let me just start out by saying, this is a, this is a historic house, it's pre-civil war, is in good shape.

342
00:28:39,338 --> 00:28:45,479
[SPEAKER_08]: And so therefore a good candidate for a single house district, you know, all the things being equal.

343
00:28:47,920 --> 00:29:04,944
[SPEAKER_08]: And it is currently under a demolition delay because the owners have proposed a major change to the roofline and the historic, they are working, the owners are working with the historical commission to, you know,

344
00:29:06,212 --> 00:29:10,115
[SPEAKER_08]: to come up with a design that is appropriate for that house.

345
00:29:11,476 --> 00:29:14,159
[SPEAKER_08]: So that's the background of 78 Cotting.

346
00:29:15,380 --> 00:29:22,446
[SPEAKER_08]: So Marianne, why don't you tell us, okay, so let's hear from the owners first.

347
00:29:23,507 --> 00:29:30,833
[SPEAKER_08]: Like given, for example, what Chris Donovan just said that the restrictions are not particularly onerous

348
00:29:32,418 --> 00:29:35,700
[SPEAKER_08]: Are you still, you still don't want the local historic district?

349
00:29:36,080 --> 00:29:36,520
[SPEAKER_08]: Is that right?

350
00:29:38,301 --> 00:29:42,083
[SPEAKER_05]: Well, we prepared a statement that we'd like to read if we may.

351
00:29:42,103 --> 00:29:42,423
[SPEAKER_05]: Oh, sure.

352
00:29:43,023 --> 00:29:43,503
[SPEAKER_08]: Absolutely.

353
00:29:43,643 --> 00:29:47,645
[SPEAKER_03]: And I don't love public speaking, so I'm going to read it and probably read it poorly.

354
00:29:47,725 --> 00:29:48,606
[SPEAKER_03]: I apologize for that.

355
00:29:48,626 --> 00:29:48,986
[SPEAKER_08]: No, no, no.

356
00:29:50,053 --> 00:29:51,113
[SPEAKER_03]: Go ahead.

357
00:29:51,133 --> 00:29:55,794
[SPEAKER_03]: We want to thank you for inviting us to join you tonight and participate in this process.

358
00:29:57,234 --> 00:29:59,855
[SPEAKER_03]: We care about Medford and its history.

359
00:30:00,855 --> 00:30:03,876
[SPEAKER_03]: We spend time at the Brooks Estate and the Oak Grove Cemetery.

360
00:30:04,716 --> 00:30:06,076
[SPEAKER_03]: We're active in local politics.

361
00:30:06,676 --> 00:30:09,597
[SPEAKER_03]: We donate to the public library and other local causes.

362
00:30:10,217 --> 00:30:14,638
[SPEAKER_03]: And we care about preserving our home's connection to the city and its history.

363
00:30:15,378 --> 00:30:21,183
[SPEAKER_03]: And that's why we hired an architect who has extensive experience working with historic homes.

364
00:30:22,043 --> 00:30:27,647
[SPEAKER_03]: That's why we've worked with him to develop a plan that respects the design and the history of our home.

365
00:30:28,428 --> 00:30:29,529
[SPEAKER_03]: His name is David Whitney.

366
00:30:29,589 --> 00:30:32,311
[SPEAKER_03]: He's here tonight and he'll be happy to talk about the ways.

367
00:30:32,331 --> 00:30:32,491
[SPEAKER_03]: Okay.

368
00:30:33,948 --> 00:30:34,428
[SPEAKER_03]: does that.

369
00:30:35,789 --> 00:30:45,175
[SPEAKER_03]: And that's why we've met with the subcommittee of the Metro Historical Commission multiple times, incorporated their feedback iteratively as we've received from them on our plans.

370
00:30:45,975 --> 00:30:52,940
[SPEAKER_03]: We are supportive of their proposal to create a plaque near our home describing its history.

371
00:30:54,100 --> 00:30:59,384
[SPEAKER_03]: We've followed the city's process for renovation for the last five months.

372
00:31:00,270 --> 00:31:02,791
[SPEAKER_03]: We've made changes, the Historical Commission has requested.

373
00:31:03,511 --> 00:31:05,532
[SPEAKER_03]: We've been open about what we're doing.

374
00:31:05,832 --> 00:31:10,974
[SPEAKER_03]: We've spoken directly to our neighbors about our plans and offered to share them with them and answer any questions they have.

375
00:31:11,955 --> 00:31:13,255
[SPEAKER_03]: We share our plans with the public.

376
00:31:13,916 --> 00:31:16,297
[SPEAKER_03]: We're at this meeting tonight to hear your concerns.

377
00:31:17,177 --> 00:31:19,538
[SPEAKER_03]: We want to do the right things the right way.

378
00:31:21,419 --> 00:31:23,780
[SPEAKER_03]: We didn't plan to renovate this home when we bought it.

379
00:31:24,040 --> 00:31:26,281
[SPEAKER_05]: Is there something you need to interject, Chris?

380
00:31:27,206 --> 00:31:27,766
[SPEAKER_08]: No, not at all.

381
00:31:27,787 --> 00:31:28,847
[SPEAKER_08]: I think that sounds great.

382
00:31:29,628 --> 00:31:31,188
[SPEAKER_03]: But that was before we had a second child.

383
00:31:31,449 --> 00:31:34,971
[SPEAKER_03]: That was before the pandemic forced us both to work from home full time.

384
00:31:36,171 --> 00:31:40,774
[SPEAKER_03]: We intend for this to be our forever home, to be here for the next however many decades.

385
00:31:41,234 --> 00:31:47,658
[SPEAKER_03]: And we need our home to evolve, to meet our needs, because it is a home, not a museum.

386
00:31:48,539 --> 00:31:56,063
[SPEAKER_03]: And we come here tonight to say that we are entirely opposed to any efforts to turn our home into a historical district.

387
00:31:58,632 --> 00:32:15,721
[SPEAKER_05]: And we would prefer to see the historical district commission focus your limited resources on the kinds of changes that are really harming Medford's character like big developers that are turning things into 12 condos with 15 parking spaces like that's not us that's not what we want to do.

388
00:32:17,543 --> 00:32:26,307
[SPEAKER_05]: I'm sure David can speak more to how our plan, even though we do change the roof line in our plan, it is very respectful of how the home is.

389
00:32:26,387 --> 00:32:27,687
[SPEAKER_05]: The color is staying the same.

390
00:32:27,707 --> 00:32:35,571
[SPEAKER_05]: I know to Brad, we've been listening, obviously, talking about whether we're using wood or composite.

391
00:32:35,611 --> 00:32:39,872
[SPEAKER_05]: We're planning to use wood for the slight porch expansion that we're doing.

392
00:32:39,892 --> 00:32:45,095
[SPEAKER_05]: I don't think that this is gonna be like a horrific

393
00:32:46,373 --> 00:32:47,654
[SPEAKER_05]: thing for our neighbors to see.

394
00:32:53,997 --> 00:32:54,278
[SPEAKER_08]: Okay.

395
00:32:54,558 --> 00:32:55,078
[SPEAKER_08]: Yes.

396
00:32:55,338 --> 00:32:56,719
[SPEAKER_08]: So that sounds good.

397
00:32:58,020 --> 00:33:04,163
[SPEAKER_08]: Certainly homeowner opposition is a major impediment to creating any local shortage.

398
00:33:04,244 --> 00:33:08,206
[SPEAKER_08]: We of course prefer to have owner approval.

399
00:33:11,140 --> 00:33:16,343
[SPEAKER_08]: So why are you opposed to creating a single house as a local historic district?

400
00:33:19,485 --> 00:33:36,393
[SPEAKER_05]: Well, what you have shared on your website, I mean, I have to say that the Medford Historical Commission website includes agendas, minutes, the Zoom link, the past videos from other meetings are all accessible.

401
00:33:38,102 --> 00:33:43,124
[SPEAKER_05]: We can't even find any of that information on the Medford Historic District Commission website.

402
00:33:44,145 --> 00:33:55,030
[SPEAKER_05]: But what is on the Medford District Commission website does not make it sound like it's a very low bar, it makes it very explicit that any changes to the roofline are

403
00:33:56,002 --> 00:33:57,103
[SPEAKER_05]: rarely approved.

404
00:33:57,223 --> 00:34:01,006
[SPEAKER_05]: I think it, I don't have the exact language in front of me, but I could look up at the website.

405
00:34:01,066 --> 00:34:03,428
[SPEAKER_05]: So right now we're, we're sitting on our bed.

406
00:34:03,448 --> 00:34:06,050
[SPEAKER_05]: This is the mini dormer right behind us.

407
00:34:06,090 --> 00:34:09,733
[SPEAKER_05]: So we have to sit scrunched together in bed so that our heads aren't hitting the ceiling.

408
00:34:10,293 --> 00:34:16,438
[SPEAKER_05]: So this is one of the places where we're hoping to slightly change the roof line so we can sit up in bed and not be touching.

409
00:34:17,299 --> 00:34:24,945
[SPEAKER_05]: Um, this is, we, we would like to be able to put our kids in bed into their crib at night without hitting our head on the ceiling.

410
00:34:25,852 --> 00:34:36,802
[SPEAKER_03]: And our plan to change the roof line does so in a way that respects the design of the house and the three members of the subcommittee of the Historical Commission have all approved it.

411
00:34:36,822 --> 00:34:40,185
[SPEAKER_03]: It actually comes from their suggestion of final design.

412
00:34:40,445 --> 00:34:42,387
[SPEAKER_03]: It's accommodated what they want us to do.

413
00:34:42,727 --> 00:34:49,173
[SPEAKER_05]: I want to just add one more thing, which I know another thing that is on the website is about things like fences.

414
00:34:49,253 --> 00:34:49,613
[SPEAKER_05]: We have

415
00:34:50,262 --> 00:35:04,232
[SPEAKER_05]: chain link fence all around our property, and we are hoping to take that chain link fence out and replace it with a wooden fence, both because it looks nicer and because black swallowwort, which is an invasive weed I'm sure you're all familiar with in Medford, is everywhere.

416
00:35:04,272 --> 00:35:12,457
[SPEAKER_05]: So we want to make a lot of these changes voluntarily, but we don't want to be forced into doing them and be restricted from any small change.

417
00:35:13,018 --> 00:35:18,982
[SPEAKER_08]: Okay, so can I just say, address a couple of your concerns?

418
00:35:19,855 --> 00:35:25,337
[SPEAKER_08]: First of all, we have not, in the time that I have been chairman, which is about 10 years, we have not said no to anyone.

419
00:35:27,438 --> 00:35:40,064
[SPEAKER_08]: We have, in some cases, worked with people to come up with mutually acceptable solutions, but we have not actually turned down a single application in the 10 years that I've been chairman.

420
00:35:44,583 --> 00:35:46,524
[SPEAKER_08]: I do apologize for the state of the website.

421
00:35:47,224 --> 00:35:50,646
[SPEAKER_08]: We just put it up about six months ago and it's still a work in progress.

422
00:35:53,708 --> 00:35:59,511
[SPEAKER_08]: And as far as, what was your other concern?

423
00:35:59,591 --> 00:36:00,031
[SPEAKER_08]: I'm sorry.

424
00:36:02,152 --> 00:36:08,915
[SPEAKER_08]: Right, yes, that is, we are not interested in any way in turning Medford into a museum.

425
00:36:10,556 --> 00:36:11,977
[SPEAKER_08]: We just, we want to,

426
00:36:12,770 --> 00:36:15,713
[SPEAKER_08]: And neither would the builders of your house want that.

427
00:36:17,975 --> 00:36:21,119
[SPEAKER_08]: We just want to preserve the historic character of Medford.

428
00:36:22,100 --> 00:36:31,850
[SPEAKER_08]: And that involves just paying some attention to design and materials and making sure that they're appropriate to the house.

429
00:36:33,019 --> 00:36:44,085
